  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Rafael Devers went 3-for-3 with a go-ahead single in the seventh, but the Giants couldn't hold the lead.",
    "what_this_means": "They held it through six innings after scoring first. The bullpen was clean through the eighth. Smith, Winn, Hentges all zeros. Then Caleb Kilian walked into the ninth and gave up three runs without recording an out. That inning was the entire game. Eleven hits and they scored three. Two on base with runners in scoring position ten times and they converted twice. The math there is what lost it.",
    "what_to_watch": "This is a team that can't afford a collapse in the ninth because the margin to work with is already thin. They had a lead. They didn't finish it. That's the tighter story here. Not that Devers had a night, but that everything he did got erased in one inning by a reliever who couldn't land a strike when it mattered.",
